    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0349" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg229"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-10-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 4, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 112.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my No. 105 of September
                    27, transmitting copies of correspondence with our consul-general at Canton and
                    with the foreign office, concerning the boycott, I now have the honor to inclose
                    herewith copy of a note which I addressed to the foreign office, under date of
                    October 3, on this matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d238-a1.xml" xpointer="d238-a1"/>
